Looking at this question: "revenue" is governed by term:Revenue, which distinguishes gross order revenue (orders.order_total, includes tax) from product revenue (order_item.revenue, excludes tax). The question says "total revenue" with no qualifier pointing to product-level, so this is material ambiguity per the term's own guidance — but the term explicitly says "Use dev.orders.order_total for gross order revenue," and location is an attribute of orders (orders.location), not of order_item directly at a clean grain distinction the question raises. Since the question is plain "total revenue" (no "product"/"beverage" qualifier), the governing term's default for unqualified "revenue" is gross order revenue.

Location grouping uses the orders model's location entity with the location label, since order_total lives on the orders model.

